      "text": "I now have a complete picture. Here is my report.\n\n---\n\n## How the tutors course JSON is fetched\n\n### The URL resolution function: `determineCourseUrl`\n\n**File:** `D:\\code\\tutors\\src\\lib\\services\\course\\services\\lo-tree.ts` (lines 162-182)\n\nThis is the core function that maps a `courseId` (from the URL path) to a `courseUrl` used for fetching. It handles three cases:\n\n1. **Full URL input** (matches a URL regex with a valid TLD) -- The input itself is used as `courseUrl`. If it contains `.netlify.app`, that suffix is stripped to derive the `courseId`.\n\n2. **Localhost / 192.x.x.x** -- Used as-is; protocol is switched to `http://`.\n\n3. **Plain course ID** (the default, and the case for `reference-course`) -- The URL is constructed by appending `.netlify.app`:\n   ```\n   return { courseId: input, courseUrl: `${input}.netlify.app` };\n   ```\n\n### The fetch call\n\n**File:** `D:\\code\\tutors\\src\\lib\\services\\course\\services\\course.svelte.ts` (line 39)\n\n```typescript\nconst response = await fetchFunction(`${courseProtocol.value}${courseUrl}/tutors.json`);\n```\n\nWhere `courseProtocol` defaults to `\"https://\"` (defined at `D:\\code\\tutors\\src\\lib\\runes.svelte.ts`, line 25).\n\n### The full URL pattern for any course\n\nCombining the protocol, the resolved `courseUrl`, and the JSON filename:\n\n```\nhttps://<courseId>.netlify.app/tutors.json\n```\n\n### The actual URL for the reference course\n\nWhen a user visits `https://next.tutors.dev/course/reference-course` (or any sub-path like `/talk/reference-course/...`), the route parameter `params.courseid` is `\"reference-course\"`. This plain string does not match the URL regex and is not localhost, so the default branch fires. The resulting fetch URL is:\n\n```\nhttps://reference-course.netlify.app/tutors.json\n```\n\nThis is the CDN/hosting URL for the reference course JSON. All course assets (images, PDFs, etc.) also resolve relative to `https://reference-course.netlify.app/`.\n\n### How assets within the course are resolved\n\n**File:** `D:\\code\\tutors\\src\\lib\\services\\course\\services\\lo-tree.ts` (lines 114-153, `injectCourseUrl`)\n\nThe raw `tutors.json` contains placeholder strings like `{{COURSEURL}}` in route, image, PDF, and video paths. After fetching, `injectCourseUrl` replaces these placeholders:\n\n- `lo.img` uses `courseUrl` (the Netlify domain), e.g. `https://reference-course.netlify.app/img/logo.png`\n- `lo.route` uses `courseId` (the plain ID), e.g. `/topic/reference-course/intro`\n- `talk.pdf` and `lab.pdf` use `courseUrl`, e.g. `https://reference-course.netlify.app/talks/intro.pdf`\n\n### Confirmation from the catalogue pruning code\n\n**File:** `D:\\code\\tutors\\src\\lib\\services\\community\\services\\catalogue.ts` (line 57)\n\n```typescript\nconst url = `https://${course.course_id}.netlify.app/tutors.json`;\n```\n\nThis independently confirms the same pattern: every course is hosted as a Netlify site at `<course_id>.netlify.app`.\n\n### Summary\n\n| Component | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Base URL pattern | `https://<courseId>.netlify.app/tutors.json` |\n| Reference course JSON URL | `https://reference-course.netlify.app/tutors.json` |\n| Protocol rune default | `\"https://\"` |\n| URL resolution function | `determineCourseUrl()` in `src/lib/services/course/services/lo-tree.ts` |\n| Fetch call | `course.svelte.ts` line 39 |\n| Asset placeholder | `{{COURSEURL}}` replaced at decoration time |",
